[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3719059366","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114678#issuecomment-3719059366","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114678","id":3719059366,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7drFem","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T14:08:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T14:08:50Z","body":"Please set up [clang-format](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/code_style.html) to fix the style locally in the future instead of running repeatedly with CI","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3719059366/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3721259511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114678#issuecomment-3721259511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114678","id":3721259511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7dzen3","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-07T23:28:12Z","updated_at":"2026-01-07T23:28:12Z","body":"This looks amazing! I have had this on the rendering team TODO list for a long time since I have long suspected that we were not culling aggressively enough. I will try to test this with project [DOGWALK](https://studio.blender.org/projects/dogwalk/) as soon as I can since that was a reasonable complex game that exhibited a pretty heavy shadow rendering bottleneck from directional lights","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3721259511/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3723239889","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114678#issuecomment-3723239889","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114678","id":3723239889,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7d7CHR","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-08T10:34:27Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T10:05:21Z","body":"Great you are looking at this. :+1: \r\n\r\nIt's a while since I wrote the PR (and even longer since I did the original which it was resurrected from, was years ago :grin: ) so it's not super fresh in memory, I remember some things were handled differently in 3.x due to the culling working differently, and 4.x was less elegant.\r\n\r\nCertainly looks like I didn't get around to culling to cascades in 4.x (can't remember if done in 3.x).\r\n\r\nI seem to remember a few considerations .. deciding how to do it more efficiently, because you have the opportunity to do e.g. one gross cull for all 4 cascades, then separate minor culls for each offset distance (or binary tree approach), rather than doing the full cull for each cascade. But it might not matter than much if the cull is relatively cheap compared to other costs, and maybe it has to be done in full to get the full benefit, I forgot the details. :blush: \r\n\r\nThe `colinear_tri` function I've completely forgotten, so would have to refresh my memory. There were certainly some bugs to work through when we added it, particularly for float error in some specific cases.\r\n\r\nEdit: see #92078","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3723239889/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3729218306","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114678#issuecomment-3729218306","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114678","id":3729218306,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eR1sC","user":{"login":"Image-unavailable","id":56268917,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MjY4OTE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56268917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable","html_url":"https://github.com/Image-unavailable","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T14:49:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T14:49:36Z","body":"Seems like I'm just going to have to run for a while a build where `_is_colinear_tri` is just `return false`, and see if it blows up.\r\n\r\nAbout performance: what I've done is essentially making the code that previously ran on the camera frustum once per directional light, run on each cascade frustum instead, so at worst it should be 4x the CPU cost as before.\r\n\r\nThe preexisting culling code was correct, it was just failing to give correct results because it was getting bad data and settings:\r\n- it was operating on the camera frustum, not the actual shadow frustum, so it:\r\n    - did not cull meshes beyond max shadow distance\r\n    - erraneously identified valid cull planes as colinear and discarded them, because the triangle made by two points on the camera's near plane (5mm apart) and one on the far plane (4km apart) is incredibly stretched\r\n- the threshold in `_is_colinear_tri` was too high, and as I wrote in a code comment: `0.001 causes false-positives with camera FOV of 70 and ortho shadows at ~50m at certain view angles.` which isn't great\r\n\r\nPassing in the correct frustums and using a smaller threshold fixed it.\r\n\r\nSo I feel like optimizing it so that 4 cascade shadows performance is instead of 4x, say, maybe 2x, wouldn't be a quick thing.\r\n\r\nEven then, 1-cascade is unoptimizable, and 2-cascade could maybe go to 1.5x. It just doesn't feel worth the effort, unless this is a major confirmed bottleneck, which I don't think it really is?\r\n\r\nIt might be possible to optimize the redundant boundcheck upstream though :thinking: (`renderer_scene_cull.cpp:3044`)\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nfor (uint32_t k = 0; k < cull_data.cull->shadows[j].cascade_count; k++) {\r\n\tif (!light_culler->cull_directional_light(cull_data.scenario->instance_aabbs[i], j, k)) { // pass the cascade index\r\n\t\tcontinue;\r\n\t}\r\n\tif (IN_FRUSTUM(cull_data.cull->shadows[j].cascades[k].frustum) && VIS_CHECK) {\r\n\t\tuint32_t base_type = idata.flags & InstanceData::FLAG_BASE_TYPE_MASK;\r\n\r\n\t\tif (((1 << base_type) & RS::INSTANCE_GEOMETRY_MASK) && idata.flags & InstanceData::FLAG_CAST_SHADOWS && \r\n\t\t\t(...)\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3729218306/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3734470776","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114678#issuecomment-3734470776","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114678","id":3734470776,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7el4B4","user":{"login":"Image-unavailable","id":56268917,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MjY4OTE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56268917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable","html_url":"https://github.com/Image-unavailable","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-11T12:10:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-11T12:10:41Z","body":"Fixed shadow flickering for omnilights near viewport edges. Seems like they need `_is_colinear_tri` with `0.001f` as threshold to work properly.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3734470776/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3762885532","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114678#issuecomment-3762885532","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114678","id":3762885532,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gSROc","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-17T08:11:01Z","updated_at":"2026-01-17T08:24:53Z","body":"> This PR fixes errors in the implementation of tight shadowcaster culling for directional lights\r\n\r\nFor clarity what errors were you referring to here BTW? As far as I could see yesterday (with the new cascade debugging view in 4.x) it appeared to be working as designed.\r\n\r\nThe epsilons chosen were pretty conservative (see #92078), partly as a result of bugs found in the wild. You may be correct that they can be different for directional versus other lights though so we can evaluate this. :+1: \r\n\r\nOn the other hand we have to consider whether there are any real world downside to overly-conservative epsilons. It just switches the tighter culling off in these situations, so potentially more objects get rendered into the shadow buffer than necessarily (same as before tighter culling was introduced). This should not introduce visual artefacts though. i.e. in culling rendering something extra is not a massive problem, whereas *not* rendering something which needs to be rendered is a much bigger problem.\r\n\r\nHaving had a bit more look at this, personally I'm of the opinion it may be worth splitting this into two PRs, as there are two changes here:\r\n\r\n* Adding the more precise culling for the cascades\r\n* Changes to epsilons\r\n\r\nGenerally it's a good idea in PRs to split them up into indivisible chunks wherever possible, so they can be examined in detail, approved on their own merit, and reverted easily.\r\n\r\nMore precise culling for cascades is something we would jump for (providing computationally efficient and not introducing artefacts). :+1: \r\n\r\nChanging epsilons is something we have to take special care with, as there are often special unforeseen cases, and it is nice to be easy to revert independently in the case of regressions.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3762885532/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3764506105","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114678#issuecomment-3764506105","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114678","id":3764506105,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gYc35","user":{"login":"Image-unavailable","id":56268917,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MjY4OTE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56268917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable","html_url":"https://github.com/Image-unavailable","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T00:04:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T00:04:52Z","body":"> For clarity what errors were you referring to here BTW? As far as I could see yesterday (with the new cascade debugging view in 4.x) it appeared to be working as designed.\r\n\r\nBasically, the existing code not culling as well as it could have. As I have written earlier in the PR:\r\n\r\n> The preexisting culling code was correct, it was just failing to give correct results because it was getting bad data and settings:\r\n> - it was operating on the camera frustum, not the actual shadow frustum, so it:\r\n>     - did not cull meshes beyond max shadow distance\r\n>     - erraneously identified valid cull planes as colinear and discarded them, because the triangle made by two points on the camera's near plane (5mm apart) and one on the far plane (4km apart) is incredibly stretched\r\n> - the threshold in `_is_colinear_tri` was too high, and as I wrote in a code comment: `0.001 causes false-positives with camera FOV of 70 and ortho shadows at ~50m at certain view angles.` which isn't great\r\n\r\n...In this case false-positives refers to meshes that could have been culled, but weren't, wasting GPU time. See images in the original PR post to see just how bad this can get. Though part of this is due to the long frustum; the epsilon is responsible for failure to cull meshes behind and sideways of the frustum, not for the meshes beyond the frustum (those are due to the long frustum).\r\n\r\n> The epsilons chosen were pretty conservative (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/92078), partly as a result of bugs found in the wild. You may be correct that they can be different for directional versus other lights though so we can evaluate this. 👍\r\n\r\nI have managed to consistently recreate severe flickering with dual-paraboloid omnis using the `0.00001f` threshold used by directionals, but directional lights don't seem to have any such negative effect to smaller values--at the very least, if they do, it's nowhere near as noticeable, since I haven't seen anything wrong with them yet.\r\n\r\nBut in my own project where I've been using a build with this PR merged, I use 4-cascade shadows, so other setups wouldn't be as tested.\r\n\r\nMaybe z-nears or FOV affect it? But with a quick test, even extreme camera z-nears (0.01) and extreme FOVs (140) seem fine.\r\n\r\n> On the other hand we have to consider whether there are any real world downside to overly-conservative epsilons. It just switches the tighter culling off in these situations, so potentially more objects get rendered into the shadow buffer than necessarily (same as before tighter culling was introduced). This should not introduce visual artefacts though. i.e. in culling rendering something extra is not a massive problem, whereas not rendering something which needs to be rendered is a much bigger problem.\r\n\r\nThe main thing with excessively large epsilons in this case is performance loss. So ideally we'd want them as tight as possible, `0.00001f` should be good for 1-cascade shadows up to the overkill range of 5000m (per cascade, at *minimum*!) before culling starts letting cullable meshes through (assuming no floating point issues).\r\n\r\nMaybe origin affects it due to floating point precision? It could since frustum corners are in world space. Idk.\r\n\r\nAs for splitting: so the first PR would declare the split constants, and the second would just set `DIRECTIONAL_LIGHT_COLINEARITY_THRESHOLD` from `0.001f` to `0.00001f`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3764506105/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765068799","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114678#issuecomment-3765068799","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114678","id":3765068799,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gamP_","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T08:48:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T10:17:35Z","body":"> As for splitting: so the first PR would declare the split constants, and the second would just set DIRECTIONAL_LIGHT_COLINEARITY_THRESHOLD from 0.001f to 0.00001f?\r\n\r\nYes, these changes are afaik independent and conceptually different, so make sense in different PRs.\r\n\r\nYou could probably e.g. just move the epsilon changes from this PR to a different PR, as they are fairly small, and leave this one to cover the cascades. I suspect the cascade stuff will likely be fine (I'd likely have done similar myself) but still need to test it a bit more when you've made the changes.\r\n\r\nEssentially you just need to modify the near and far plane for the camera frustum for each cascade, if I remember right, which I think you are doing here.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765068799/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3773204595","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114678#issuecomment-3773204595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114678","id":3773204595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7g5ohz","user":{"login":"Image-unavailable","id":56268917,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MjY4OTE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56268917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable","html_url":"https://github.com/Image-unavailable","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Image-unavailable/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/us